# per-target resume checkpoints — must survive `git clean -fd`
results/*.jsonl
!results/*.md

# THE ONE CHECKPOINT A CLONE CANNOT DO WITHOUT.
#
# The rule above is right for run state: n_scaling_ckpt.jsonl is 2.4 MB,
# null_control_ckpt_defb.jsonl 236 KB, rescore_likelihoods_ckpt.jsonl 635 KB, and every
# rebuild that consumes them ALSO needs data/cache/, which is ignored wholesale at line 47.
# Shipping them would not make those rebuilds runnable from a clone; they would still exit
# non-zero on the missing cache, which is a loud, honest failure.
#
# The winner's-curse checkpoint is the exception on both counts. It is 19 KB, and
# `winners_curse_reeval.py --report_only` reads NOTHING but the checkpoint — it is the only
# no-GPU rebuild in this repo that is self-contained from a fresh clone. Leaving it ignored
# did not fail loudly, it failed QUIETLY: the retired 60-record `_def` file was tracked (it
# predates this rule), the script defaulted to it, and the documented rebuild overwrote
# results/winners_curse_se_false_alarm.md with retention 45.2% [25%, 65%] in place of the
# paper's 44% [23%, 64%], exit code 0.
#
# The glob covers both files deliberately: the retired `_def` checkpoint and the definitive
# `_defb` one have to travel together, or the marker below names a file that isn't there.
#
# NOTE FOR WHOEVER COMMITS THIS: un-ignoring makes the file untracked-and-not-ignored, which
# `git clean -fd` DELETES. `git add results/winners_curse_ckpt_se_false_alarm_defb.jsonl` in
# the same commit. (This cell is finished, not in-progress: 69 of 80 targets, the other 11
# skipped because the optimiser found no paraphrase to re-test.)
!results/winners_curse_ckpt_*.jsonl

# Machine-readable retirement notices that sit beside a checkpoint, e.g.
# results/winners_curse_ckpt_se_false_alarm_def.jsonl.SUPERSEDED.json. `results/*.json`
# (line 48) would otherwise swallow them. A .jsonl cannot carry the `> SUPERSEDED` banner
# the .md reports carry, so this sidecar IS the banner and must ship with the data it
# retires — an ignored retirement notice is the same defect as no notice at all.
!results/*.SUPERSEDED.json

# the equivalence-audit sheet, key and labels are EVIDENCE, not derived output.
# results/*.csv above would have silently excluded them, which breaks the
# transparency-in-place-of-inter-annotator-kappa argument the protocol rests on.
!results/equivalence_audit*.csv

# Runtime status surfaces -- rewritten every 15 s by the stop watcher and every 300 s by the
# progress monitor. Tracking them makes the tree permanently dirty and invites an accidental
# commit of whatever a background agent happened to be mid-write on.
dashboard/session_status.json
dashboard/session_status.js
dashboard/progress_status.json
dashboard/progress_samples.jsonl
dashboard/*.stdout
dashboard/*.err
dashboard/stop_watcher*.log
dashboard/overnight_*.log
